{
	"openapi": "3.0.3",
	"info": {
		"title": "BTClock API",
		"version": "3.4.0",
		"description": "BTClock V3 HTTP API as implemented by the firmware `src/lib/net/webserver/` module.\nREST routes are under `/api/...`; SSE lives at `/events`; OTA uploads use `/upload/...`.\nThe embedded WebUI may rewrite `/api` to `/` for same-origin routing.\n\n## 3.4.0 breaking changes\n\n- State-changing routes moved from `GET` to `POST`. The legacy `GET`\n  forms (e.g. `GET /api/identify`, `GET /api/restart`,\n  `GET /api/action/pause`, `GET /api/full_refresh`,\n  `GET /api/show/*`, `GET /api/lights/*`, `GET /api/frontlight/*`) are\n  no longer registered.\n- Settings writes moved from `PATCH /api/json/settings` to\n  `PATCH /api/settings`. The old URL is gone.\n- `POST /api/show/custom` and `POST /api/lights/set` are POST-only;\n  the firmware no longer accepts PATCH on those routes.\n- The `customEndpoint` settings key is retired \u2014 use `ceEndpoint`\n  instead (there is no migration shim).\n- `GET /api/settings` no longer returns plaintext passwords; see the\n  `Settings` schema for the `httpAuthPassSet` / `otaPassSet`\n  booleans.\n\n## Validation errors\n\n`PATCH /api/settings` returns `400 Bad Request` with a JSON body\n`{ \"error\": \"<field>:<reason>\" }` when a value fails validation \u2014\nsee the response definition on that endpoint for the full\nvocabulary. The WebUI's `parseSettingsError` helper splits this\ninto `{ field, reason }` so the offending input can be highlighted\nand scrolled into view.\n\n## Auth\n\nWhen the device has `httpAuthEnabled = true`, *every* endpoint on this\nspec requires HTTP Basic auth, including the SSE stream and read-only\nstatus endpoints. When it is false (the factory default), no endpoint\nrequires auth. The auth contract is the same on all routes so it is\nonly called out explicitly here rather than duplicated per-path.\n"
	},
	"servers": [
		{
			"url": "/"
		}
	],
