		"/events": {
			"get": {
				"tags": ["system"],
				"summary": "Server-Sent Events stream of status updates",
				"description": "Event stream for live status updates. The firmware emits three\nkinds of frames over the wire:\n\n- `event: welcome` \u2014 sent once on connect; payload is the\n  stringified IP address of the client.\n- `event: status` \u2014 payload JSON matches `GET /api/status`\n  (shares `buildStatusJson()`). One frame is pushed on every\n  state change (block height update, screen rotation, LED\n  colour change, DND transition, etc.).\n- `data: closing` (no `event:` prefix, default `message`\n  listener) \u2014 sent immediately before the firmware closes the\n  connection cleanly (e.g. when the LFS image is being swapped\n  during an OTA finalisation). Clients should reconnect after\n  a short delay; this is a graceful handoff, not a failure.\n\nReconnect strategy: 1 s on first `error`, doubling to a 30 s\ncap (see `src/lib/api/sse.ts::computeBackoffMs` in the WebUI),\nand 5 s after a `closing` message. The \"lost connection\"\noverlay reads its label from `statusStore.otaInProgress` so\nusers see \"Updating firmware\u2026\" during an OTA reconnect.\n",
				"security": [
					{
						"basicAuth": []
					}
				],
				"responses": {
					"200": {
						"description": "text/event-stream"
					}
				}
			}
		}
	},
	"components": {
		"securitySchemes": {
			"basicAuth": {
				"type": "http",
				"scheme": "basic"
			}
		},
		"schemas": {
			"ConnectionStatus": {
				"type": "object",
				"properties": {
					"price": {
						"type": "boolean"
					},
					"blocks": {
						"type": "boolean"
					},
					"V2": {
						"type": "boolean"
					},
					"nostr": {
						"type": "boolean"
					}
				}
			},
			"DndNestedStatus": {
				"type": "object",
				"description": "DND block embedded in `GET /api/status` and SSE payload",
